  "notes": {
    "instance": "Captured against a throwaway second instance of THIS checkout (tools/panel-testkit.mjs startPanel): free port, own PANEL_CONFIG and own store under the scratch dir, assistant/gateway off. It serves public/app.js and public/style.css byte-identical to this tree (hashes in environment.servedFiles). The live panel on 7331 serves a different build and was not touched.",
    "board": "The sandbox config carries no projects (projects: []), so the board behind the Settings window is empty. That is why shots[*].file (the full-page record) is not pixel-comparable with the baseline's full-page shot; the Settings window is, and its rect is recorded in shots[*].win so the compare stage can diff that region out of each full-page shot.",
    "shotPair": "shots[*].file is a full-page record with the Settings window at its recorded win rect; shots[*].surfaceFile is the 340x520 Settings window alone and is the stable pair to diff. Every pair here has the same viewport, state, steps and asserts as its baseline counterpart.",
    "servedIndex": "The served public/index.html differs from the tree only by the panel's cache-busting stamp (?v=<panel-build> on stylesheet links and a meta panel-build tag); app.js and style.css are byte-identical to this tree."
  },
